          "question": "e-4408",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $I_3$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
